    {
      "jobId": "5cf3b6e9-de56-4f90-b1d6-4a82bb654e91",
      "question": "Among the 50 most liquid US stocks, which had the strongest and weakest returns over the 20 trading sessions ending March 12, 2026, and how did their daily volatility compare?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T18:34:57.288532Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T18:35:15.711700Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Top 50 most liquid US stocks — 20 trading sessions ending March 12, 2026**\n\n| Rank | Ticker | Return | Daily Volatility |\n|------|--------|--------|------------------|\n| **Strongest returns** | | | |\n| 1 | CRCL | +97.37% | 8.86% |\n| 2 | COIN | +26.88% | 6.54% |\n| 3 | NFLX | +18.32% | 3.82% |\n| **Weakest returns** | | | |\n| 1 | BABA | –18.45% | 1.79% |\n| 2 | GS | –16.63% | 2.57% |\n| 3 | CRWV | –16.11% | 6.36% |\n\n*Returns are measured from the close before the window’s first session to the close of March 12, 2026. Volatility is the standard deviation of daily returns over the same 20 sessions.* [1][2]\n\n**Volatility comparison**\nThe strongest performers (CRCL, COIN) showed notably higher daily volatility (6.5–8.9%) than the weakest performers BABA and GS (1.8–2.6%), while CRWV’s volatility (6.4%) was similar to the leaders. This pattern is descriptive, not predictive, and does not imply a causal link between volatility and return direction over this window.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:90b258cc06e96efdba043341c6756bb9483b2131bff2e85bc5b4bbdff57a7545`\n- [2] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:d566e9eb3837fd970ddc363c4728ae70f3efb0b60913f4b4cd3f3aa9bd52d158`",
